Combining the above, with the phase space factor (PSF) and the BW function, we write the following function to fit the \(K\pi\) invariant mass spectrum.

\[f(M_{K\pi})=BW(M_{K\pi})\times PSF(M_{K\pi})+RBG(M_{K\pi}) \tag{4.17}\]

in which, \(Y\), \(B\), \(C\), \(M_{K^{*}}\) and \(\Gamma_{K^{*}}\) are five open parameters with their usual meaning. We can now extract the mass and width of the \(K^{*}(892)\) from the fit.

